<title>UK: L-Bank unit sets 750 million mark five-year bond.</title>
<headline>L-Bank unit sets 750 million mark five-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Goldman Sachs International and SBC Warburg on Thursday.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BADEN-WUERTTEMBERG L-FINANCE NV</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  L-BANK</p>
<p> AMT    750 MLN DEM   COUPON     **	  MATURITY    26.SEP.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    26.SEP.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+22 BP</p>
<p> NOTES    **TO BE PRICED LATER</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    FRA/STUT  PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMS US/UK/DE/NL</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 1</p>
<p> GOV LAW    GERMAN    HOME CTRY  GERMANY   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  1.75	PRAECIP     NONE</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND OBL 119 -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
